Folding
dadi considers the data in the spectrum to be polarized, and ancestral state of each variant is known. If this insn't possible, need to fold the FS using:
folded = fs.fold()

Projection
can project an FS down from larger sample size to smaller size. Averages over all possible re-samplings of the larger sample size. Often done in the case of missing data. Missing data can include: if some sites could not be called in all individuals, one can set a lower bound on the number of successfull calls necessary to include a SNP in the analysis; SNPs with more successful calls can then be projected down to that number of calls
To project a two D FS down to saple sizes of 14 and 26 use: 
proj = fs.project([14, 26])

